{
  "id": "ss.relic.drone-cannibal",
  "name": "Cannibal brood",
  "description": "A fed grub — amber, the colour `ss.proj.chip` goes when it has eaten — with its jaws in the near side of a split carapace, and a new grub, still the near-white of a fresh one, coming out of the far side of the same husk. The relic makes a grub that kills leave another grub in the corpse, so the corpse is the middle of the drawing and the two grubs are its before and after. Both bodies are legless grubs, thin at the tail and round at the head, with segment lines and a pair of pale jaws and nothing else on them: no eyes, no dark head-dot, because a dark spot in a pale round head is an eye looking at you. It stays off ss.relic.drone by having no egg: that one is three young in a shell, this is one young going into a body.",
